          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The absolute refractive index of a medium is simply called its refractive index. The refractive index of several media is given in Table 9.3. From",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " the Table you can know that the refractive index of water, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n _ { _ w } = 1 . 3 3 ."
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " This means that the ratio of the speed of light in air and the speed of light in water is equal to 1.33. Similarly, the refractive index of crown glass, "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "n _ { _ { q } }   =   1 . 5 2"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": ".",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Such data are helpful in many places. However, you "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "need not memorise the data.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
